 ## Groups and group chats
 
+This installation adds an opt-in `hosted_rooms.owner_aliases` mapping in the
+root `config.yaml` for an operator who uses both native Desktop and a dashboard
+login. Map the exact authenticated subject to the native subject, for example
+`'auth:v1:["basic","","your-login"]': 'uid:501'`. Restart the gateway after
+changing the mapping. Group authorization compares these explicitly linked
+identities; existing room IDs, owners, logs and member task identities stay
+unchanged. Other authenticated users retain their separate rooms.
+
+This installation also supports `hosted_rooms.shared_directory: true` in the
+root configuration. Host-scoped connections then list all authorized rooms on
+the served profiles as one paginated collection. Room-ID operations route to
+the original owning profile, including existing rooms opened from a different
+foreground profile. Profile-bound grants keep their original scope. Duplicate
+room IDs across profiles are refused as ambiguous; rooms and logs are never
+copied, merged or moved. Restart the gateway after changing this setting.
+
+The canonical room composer reuses the mention input: Enter sends, Shift+Enter
+adds a newline, and composition Enter does not send unfinished IME text. The
+group model picker uses the existing model catalog. Apply stores one selection
+for future responses of every local member in that room (`groups.model`); it
+does not change the bots' profile configuration or their other chats. Existing
+member sessions use the canonical model mutation and its guards. Members with
+no group session inherit the selection at their first real turn. The server
+stores the selection in state_meta and shares it in `groups.state`.
+
